welcome back to new rock stars i'm  whitney van laningham and my biggest  question after watching the multiverse  of madness is did scarlet witch get  scarlet squished or was she somehow able  to survive an entire temple collapsing  on top of her it certainly wouldn't be  the first time that she lived through  impossible odds including the explosion  that killed her parents and the  torturer's experiments from hydra but  will we really see 616's scarlet witch  again or is rwanda dead in the aftermath  of the multiverse of madness premiere  elizabeth olsen has been busy giving  interviews about the fate of her  character back in march rumors were  circulating that she'd extended her  contract with marvel and although she  didn't explicitly state that she had she  did tell collider that she doesn't see  this as the end for her character and  hinted that her mcu contracts are always  adjusting in another interview with  variety she seemed super excited for the  possibility of returning to the screen  saying it's weird that i'm expecting to  return but no one's told me i'm doing  anything but in my mind i'm just making  the assumption that they'll have me  again i don't know to what capacity but  i hope i'm back i hope there's also more  fun to be had in something different  where do we go i feel like we've done so  much with her it's been really a wild  couple years with her if lizzy's down to  keep going i am too so let's talk about  what those different fun directions  might be wanda maximoff is one of the  most powerful and fascinating characters  in the mcu and with the immense success  of wandavision she's become one of the  most popular characters in the entire  series not only is she the only avenger  who could have single-handedly defeated  thanos a rare wielder of chaos magic and  the scarlet witch she was also the only  being in the multiverse powerful enough  to take herself out even strange wong in  america knew that there was no way to  physically stop her they could only  continue to reason with her until she  made the choice on her own and if she's  capable of all that i'd be willing to  bet that she was able to keep herself  alive at the end of multiverse of  madness too but let's look deeper at  some of the evidence i think it's  totally possible that wanda will return  this wouldn't be the first time that  wanda was presumed dead in marvel  history in fact in the house of m  storyline which multiverse of madness  draws inspiration from wanda disappears  after altering reality to remove all  mutants from the world she's presumed  dead and doctor strange even suggests  that she may have taken her own life but  hawkeye later finds her living in mount  undergore with zero memory of what  happened or that she even had powers at  all and it makes a lot of sense for them  to make it seem like wanda is gone in  the mcu too with her off the chessboard  marvel has time to build up newer larger  threats in her absence the scarlet witch  could pretty much take out anyone so  with big bads like gore and kang on the  horizon they needed to take wanda out in  the multiverse of madness to keep things  interesting kevin feige knows his timing  and in my opinion i think her death was  the best way to move her story forward  when wanda destroyed the temple at  wundegar in this film a large red flash  of light shoots out of the actively  decimating rebel and while you could  arguably view this scene as confirmation  that the scarlet witch's life force was  extinguished from the 616 reality i also  think that there's a valid argument that  this flash of light proves she's still  alive at every single pivotal point in  her life thus far wanda has protected  herself even if she didn't realize at  the time that she was intentionally  doing it for example when agatha makes  her relive the night her parents died  she notes that wanda subconsciously used  a probability hex to prevent the bomb  from going off she protests saying that  the bomb was just effective but agatha  continues to point out further instances  of her doing similar things she was also  the first test subject of hydras to  survive direct contact with an infinity  stone and her love for vision  unintentionally created an entire town  to soothe her own broken heart agatha  points out that her chaos magic  amplified by the mind stone allowed her  to survive these experiences and i think  it's possible that she survived this one  too whether she meant to or not i think  that that red light signifies her chaos  magic protecting her yet again and if  she does come back in future marvel  properties we could find her lost in the  ruins of mount undergore without her  powers or her memories just like they  did in the comics you never want your  earbuds to fall out whether you're just  walking the dog exercising or bumping  around the house blasting your favorite  episode of the dungeons and daddies  podcast without your loved ones being  like whitney ron stampler isn't a real  person recon's everyday earbuds have  optimized gel tips for the perfect fit  it makes them comfortable and they don't  budge thanks to raycon for sponsoring  this video  holy diver you've been down too long in  the midnight sea  wow that totally worked look at them  look at them they're still in my head  they're still firmly in my head raycon's  everyday earbuds look feel and sound  better than ever they offer 8 hours of  play time and a 32 32-hour battery life  that's long enough to listen to the tale  of four dads rescuing their sons from  the forgotten realms raycons are priced  so that you get quality audio at half  the price of other premium audio brands  it's no wonder raycon's everyday earbuds  have over forty nine 5 star reviews and  they come with a 45 day happiness  guarantee click the link in the  description or go to buyreicon.com  new rockstars to get 15 off your recon  purchase once again go to byraycon.com  new rockstars for 15 off there have also  been rumors floating around that wanda  might appear in house of harkness  alongside her nemesis from westview but  elizabeth olsen stated in an interview  that she doesn't think that she signed  up for that series judging by the way  she's enthusiastically expressed her  openness for other potential storylines  i'd say she's not garfielding here for  example in an interview with  comicbook.com she said that she'd really  like to see a storyline where we see the  scarlet witch as an aging woman she said  quote there are a few images in my head  of i think they're from witches row and  she's aging into kane while using her  power and there's something in that this  older woman who's aging from her power  that i'm interested in and i don't  really know what that means but i kind  of would love to be old elizabeth olsen  also seems extremely interested in doing  more with the house of m storyline even  saying quote i do think doctor strange  too opens up lots of opportunities with  the multiverse but yeah the immortal  words are no more mutants i mean i would  love to be able to say them in some  capacity to make it work for the mcu and  i know i know this is an actor  discussing hypothetical work that she'd  love to be a part of not an official  confirmation from kevin feige that this  is definitely gonna happen but she said  it herself mom really opened us up for a  lot of possibilities for what could  happen to her character in the future so  i'm not taking wanda reappearing for  more of this story inspired by house of  m off the table playing a version of  herself that's stripped of her abilities  or has her powers redefined in a new  context might give the scarlet witch the  ability to come back to the 616 verse  without forcing fans to just forgive and  forget the destruction she caused as of  right now it's a little hard to get past  the murderous rampage she went on in  multiverse of madness but if wanda were  able to start over in the 616 with a  clean slate see